    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0993" n="979" xml:id="pg979"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/8–2344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-23T09:00:00+07:00">August 23, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1449. According to local chief representative of China Defense Supplies in
                    liquidation, that organization is being terminated (our 1276, July 22) and China
                    lend-lease matters at this end are to be handled by Transport Commission or
                    Military Affairs Commission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
